<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  LANraragi Reader — Network Security Configuration

  WHY CLEARTEXT IS GLOBALLY ALLOWED HERE:

  LANraragi servers are typically reached via bare LAN IPs over plain HTTP
  (e.g., http://192.168.1.23:3000). Android's <domain-config> cannot match
  CIDR ranges or wildcard IPs, and we do not know which IP a given user has
  configured at install time. We therefore must allow cleartext at the OS
  level for ALL hosts.

  WHERE THE REAL CLEARTEXT POLICY LIVES:

  The authoritative cleartext gate is `LRRCleartextRejectionInterceptor`
  (client/api/). It refuses an HTTP request unless its host:port and scheme
  belong to a configured profile (or, before the profile cache is loaded, to
  the active server) AND either the user consented to plain HTTP for that
  profile (`allowCleartext`, the "trust this server over plain HTTP" box) or
  the host is a LAN address (`LRRUrlHelper.isLanAddress`: localhost, *.local,
  and private / link-local / 100.64/10 IP literals).

  Net effect at runtime: cleartext goes only to configured servers — any of
  them, not just the active one — and a LAN server needs no consent. On a
  foreign network that reuses the same private range, the API key is sent in
  the clear to whatever answers at that address; the UI labels such profiles
  "Unencrypted (HTTP)" (audit 2026-10-04 C27 / SEC-21).

  TRUST ANCHORS (release vs debug):
    base-config       → system CAs only
    debug-overrides   → system + user CAs (Charles, mitmproxy, etc.)

  Release builds do NOT trust user-installed CAs. If you need to point a
  release build at a self-signed HTTPS LANraragi server, install the CA
  via the system trust store. There is no in-app CA import or certificate
  pinning yet (audit C27 phase 2).
-->
<network-security-config>

    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true">
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="system"/>
        </trust-anchors>
    </base-config>

    <debug-overrides>
        <trust-anchors>
            <certificates src="user"/>
        </trust-anchors>
    </debug-overrides>

</network-security-config>
